{"name":"Nymphaeaceae","hex":"#cee0e3","fetched":"2026-10-12","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"Nymphaeaceae","whole":true,"parts":[{"part":"Proper noun","definitions":["A taxonomic family within the order Nymphaeales – the water lilies."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/Nymphaeaceae"}],"entries":[{"title":"Nymphaeaceae","blocks":[{"text":"Nymphaeaceae is a family of flowering plants, commonly called water lilies. They live as rhizomatous aquatic herbs in temperate and tropical climates around the world. The family contains five genera with about 70 known species. Water lilies are rooted in soil in bodies of water, with leaves and flowers floating on or rising from the surface. Leaves are oval and heart-shaped in Barclaya. Leaves are round, with a radial notch in Nymphaea and Nuphar, but fully circular in Victoria and Euryale."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/1/11/Nymphaea_nouchali5.JPG/330px-Nymphaea_nouchali5.JPG?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Nymphaeaceae","wikidata":"Q148650"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/1/16/Barclaya_longifolia_in_Thailand_crooped.jpg/500px-Barclaya_longifolia_in_Thailand_crooped.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/1/16/Barclaya_longifolia_in_Thailand_crooped.jpg/500px-Barclaya_longifolia_in_Thailand_crooped.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"Flowering Barclaya longifolia specimen, Thailand","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3ABarclaya_longifolia_in_Thailand_crooped.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/2/2f/Victoria_cruziana_flower.jpg/330px-Victoria_cruziana_flower.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/